Cell[TextData[{
 "The same cat state, two quasi-probabilities. The Wigner on the left has the \
two Gaussian lobes at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", "\[PlusMinus]", "2", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b649e79-a2e1-7610-291b-1022d6945d7a"],
 ", the coherent components, together with the interference ridge oscillating \
above and below zero between them; that negativity is the signature of the \
superposition. The Husimi on the right keeps only the two smooth, \
non-negative lobes, each near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "2", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09cb884c-5fc8-b209-3fc8-22165a620153"],
 ", with the fringes smoothed flat. Both are properly normalized \
quasi-probabilities, the Wigner integrating to ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "376c6589-bcca-29e8-5d14-7cd3357f7b32"],
 " over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "667bb688-7420-22c7-0e18-2fd27dd5702d"],
 " and the Husimi to ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72002252-da4c-5210-223f-c41fdff9217a"],
 " over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "084561a7-5440-aaee-387b-78015dfaf834"],
 " (equivalently, to ",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "721e71e5-9ca7-ded5-2226-68cf1553a43f"],
 " over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a84e7eb-55e0-1894-3abb-feb563956afe"],
 "), but only the Wigner can take negative values, which is why Wigner \
negativity, and not the always-positive Husimi, is the witness of \
nonclassicality. Decoherence erases the Wigner fringes and leaves the lobes, \
moving the left picture toward the right."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3261920b-7b77-02d6-621e-14557e02503c"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Every object carries its basis", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"4ebe3b2c-9c8f-bd2d-7645-b376153b0477"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The scope extends inward as well: every state, operator, and measurement \
above is stored together with the basis it is written in. A basis is a stored \
matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d6a0058-fb4a-caff-2b69-9a05fefc98c5"],
 " whose rows are the basis vectors in computational coordinates, a change of \
basis is the similarity transformation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[ScriptCapitalB]"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["B", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41d92934-9aba-8299-77e6-c17e1f4cd0e3"],
 ", and objects written in different bases reconcile automatically through \
the computational frame. About three dozen named bases are provided (Bell, \
Fourier, Schwinger, Dirac, Gell-Mann, Wigner, MUB, SIC), and the same \
mechanism converts non-computational measurements for OpenQASM export and \
supplies the Bell-derived basis used in two-qubit KAK gate compilation. The \
representation changes while the physics does not: take the qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"+"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5cc23ff5-bf0f-f019-04f1-b6bf3abbc363"],
 ", the superposition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"0"},
      "Ket"], "+", 
     TemplateBox[{"1"},
      "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29880975-91f0-008f-5fb7-a13f278552d5"],
 " in the computational basis, and write it in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "551c00cf-fc58-99c4-0323-99a8f5d2eb2e"],
 " basis instead:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"22235db8-54be-42b7-53d1-54e25d4b109d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<+\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<X\>\""}], 
   "]"}], " ", "//", " ", "TraditionalForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[73]:=",ExpressionUUID->"0976d5ae-737d-f257-3f0d-cc080609c0bd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  InterpretationBox[
   TooltipBox[
    StyleBox[
     FormBox[
      InterpretationBox[
       StyleBox[
        TemplateBox[{
          RowBox[{
            FormBox[
             SubscriptBox["\"\[ScriptX]\"", 
              InterpretationBox["\"+\"", 1]], TraditionalForm]}]},
         "Ket"],
        FontWeight->"Plain"],
       Wolfram`QuantumFramework`QuditName[
        Subscript["\[ScriptX]", 
         Interpretation["+", 1]], "Dual" -> False]],
      TraditionalForm],
     ShowStringCharacters->False],
    TagBox[
     GridBox[{{"\"X\""}, {
        TemplateBox[{"\"QuantumState: \"", 
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", "}"}], "\[Rule]", 
            RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}]}, "RowDefault"]}}, 
      GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Center}}}, DefaultBaseStyle -> 
      "Column", 
      GridBoxItemSize -> {
       "Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}], "Column"]],
   Wolfram`QuantumFramework`QuantumState[
   SparseArray[Automatic, {2}, 0, {1, {{0, 1}, {{1}}}, {1}}], 
    Wolfram`QuantumFramework`QuantumBasis[<|
     "Input" -> Wolfram`QuantumFramework`QuditBasis[<|{
           
           Wolfram`QuantumFramework`QuditName[\[FormalCapitalI], "Dual" -> 
            False], 1} -> 1|>], "Output" -> 
      Wolfram`QuantumFramework`QuditBasis[<|{
           Wolfram`QuantumFramework`QuditName[
            Subscript["\[ScriptX]", 
             Interpretation["+", 1]], "Dual" -> False], 1} -> 
         SparseArray[
          Automatic, {2}, 0, {
           1, {{0, 2}, {{1}, {2}}}, {2^Rational[-1, 2], 2^Rational[-1, 2]}}], {
           Wolfram`QuantumFramework`QuditName[
            Subscript["\[ScriptX]", 
             Interpretation["\[Minus]", -1]], "Dual" -> False], 1} -> 
         SparseArray[
          Automatic, {2}, 0, {
           1, {{0, 2}, {{1}, {2}}}, {
            2^Rational[-1, 2], -2^Rational[-1, 2]}}]|>], "Picture" -> 
      "Schrodinger", "Label" -> "X", "ParameterSpec" -> {}|>]]], 
  TraditionalForm]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9948953561616173`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[73]//TraditionalForm=",ExpressionUUID->"8b64ccc4-3686-47f5-bd48-\
3de7ab8effb2"]
